   Infant Anthropology and conceptions of Environmental Anthropology of Tim
   Ingold in order to think about the yard of school as a breeding ground
   to the experiences and the suitable discoveries of babies and small
   children. Is considered that the ethnographic experience on
   horizontality with newborns and infants in the school's backyard
   provides grants to amplify the discussion theoretical-methodology of the
